          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-56123"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "socat versions 1.8.0.0 through 1.8.1.1 contain a heap-based buffer overflow vulnerability that allows a malicious SOCKS5 proxy server to overwrite adjacent heap memory by exploiting a sign-extension flaw in the DOMAINNAME reply parser. During connection setup, the domain name length byte is read through a signed char field causing a negative bytes_to_read value that is implicitly converted to size_t, resulting in an unbounded heap write into the 262-byte reply buffer with attacker-controlled size and content.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
